--- body ---
## Context

Observed in the 2026-10-02 raid on 0853/0937/0979/1014 (PRs #1129-#1132).
The raid's Imagine/Plan/Feasibility phases append annotation log lines to
ticket files and commit them on main between executor spawns. Four executor
agents then branched at different moments while parallel sessions advanced
main, so the same annotation patch existed as three distinct commits
(26c8ab73 native, 635cf70c cherry-picked, and reproduced inline in the #1132
executor's conflict resolution). Git cannot use patch-equivalence as a merge
base, so every pair of wave PRs carrying different SHAs of the same patch
collided on the ticket files at merge time (verified pairwise by the wave
integration review with git merge-tree).

Cost during the raid: one wave-PR rebase to drop a duplicate, one full manual
rebase of #1132 with conflict resolution across three ticket files, and one
rebase redo after origin/main advanced again mid-merge. No content was lost,
but every conflict was a bookkeeping artifact, not a substantive disagreement.

## Actions

1. In the raid skill, land the wave's ticket annotations as ONE commit before
   Phase 5 spawns executors, and require every wave branch to base on it (the
   way the verify-adherence annotations already ride the first merge today).
   If a parallel session advances main mid-wave, the wave rebases the shared
   annotation commit once, together — never per-branch.
2. Alternatively or additionally: move raid-phase annotations out of the
   shared tickets/ files entirely during the wave (a sidecar log collected
   into the tickets at wrap-up), so mid-wave merges cannot collide on them.
   Decide the smaller mechanism, not both.

## Test

A wave of two or more PRs branched after the fix must show no ticket-file
conflict at merge time when the annotation commit is an ancestor of every
wave branch (mechanically: git merge-tree pairwise clean).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The raid skill's annotation flow produces one shared, mergeable base
      for all wave branches, or annotations land outside the shared files
      during the wave
- [ ] The chosen mechanism is documented where the raid skill phases
      describe ticket commits

## Invariants

- Ticket log lines stay append-only and attributed (2026-10-02 raid
  annotations all reached main intact, just via conflict-prone paths).
